Smart Research Assistant
Developed a Python-based NLP application to summarize technical articles and answer questions from the given content.
Used Transformer models (FLAN-T5 & TinyLlama) for text summarization and question answering.
Built and deployed the prototype using Streamlit, gaining practical experience in NLP, Transformers, prompt engineering and AI application development.













🤖 Smart Research Assistant — 4 Important Points

1. What I used:

“I developed a Smart Research Assistant using Python, Pandas, Hugging Face Transformers and PyTorch, with transformer models such as FLAN-T5 and TinyLlama.”

2. What the project does:

“The system takes technical articles and can summarize the content and answer questions based on the article, helping users understand lengthy information quickly.”

3. Outcome:

“We found that TinyLlama handled targeted question-answering effectively, while FLAN-T5 had limitations with longer text. We also deployed the prototype using Streamlit and Hugging Face Spaces.”

4. Skills I learned: ⭐

“Through this project, I learned NLP, Transformer models, prompt engineering, text summarization, question answering, model inference with PyTorch, and Streamlit deployment.”

🔥 One-line ending

“The key learning from this project was how Generative AI can convert large amounts of unstructured text into concise information and useful answers.”

The notebook specifically describes the project as addressing information overload and concludes that the Streamlit interface supports summarization and insight extraction for better decision-making.